From 0c048c6676819d6ab36ddfadd1391f6bb43094a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:19:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] kboot: allow up to 16 /arm-io/i2c devices

The J716s ADT has nine I2C controllers, i2c0 to i2c8.
dt_disable_missing_devs() takes at most eight, so kboot_prepare_dt()
failed with "ADT: too many /arm-io/i2c devices" and m1n1 fell back to
the proxy instead of booting the kernel. Raise the limit to 16. Only
the size of two temporary arrays changes; the lookup is the same.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
---
 src/kboot.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
index a75b5e9..f7affff 100644
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -6979,7 +6979,8 @@ int kboot_prepare_dt(void *fdt)
         return -1;
     if (dt_disable_missing_devs("acio", "cio@", 8, 2))
         return -1;
-    if (dt_disable_missing_devs("i2c", "i2c@", 8, 0))
+    /* T6050 has nine I2C controllers (i2c0..i2c8) */
+    if (dt_disable_missing_devs("i2c", "i2c@", 16, 0))
         return -1;
     if (dt_disable_missing_j700_touch_id())
         return -1;
